# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown
# `CONNECTOR-IDENTITY-KEY`: every way an id-form `bundle` member can fail, one per
# line, each naming what the author wrote.
#
# Section 2 exists for the CROSS-SECTION case, and the answer it pins is that
# there is no special diagnostic for it. Ids are unique per SECTION (core §1)
# and a cross-section reference is a line error by design, so an id declared in
# a neighbouring section arrives as an id this section never declared — which
# is what the message says, in the words that are true for it. Inventing a
# "declared in another section" message would be inventing a resolution model
# the language does not have.
figdown 0.5 topology
node a "A"
node b "B"
node c "C"
edge a -- b id=l1
edge a -- c
# an id that names nothing
bundle b1 "B1" l1,ghost
# an id that names a NODE — a bundle collects links, not endpoints
bundle b2 "B2" a
# the same connector twice, once by id and once by pair: `MEMBER-LIST-DUPLICATION`'s duplicate rule
# binds to the RESOLVED edge, so it catches the mixture with no rule of its own
bundle b3 "B3" l1,a--b
# a bare member that is not a legal id at all
bundle b4 "B4" l1,a.b
# an id that names a BUNDLE
bundle b5 "B5" b1

figdown 0.5 topology
node d "D"
node e "E"
edge d -- e id=far
# `l1` is declared in section 1 and is not in scope here
bundle b6 "B6" far,l1
